  "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel.\nAn attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system.\nThis update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:\n  - Multiple devices driver;\n  - eXpress Data Path;\n  - Kernel build system;\n  - ARM64 architecture;\n  - PowerPC architecture;\n  - RISC-V architecture;\n  - S390 architecture;\n  - x86 architecture;\n  - Block layer subsystem;\n  - Intel NPU Driver;\n  - Compute Acceleration Framework;\n  - ACPI drivers;\n  - Drivers core;\n  - Ublk userspace block driver;\n  - Bus devices;\n  - Hardware random number generator core;\n  - Clock framework and drivers;\n  - Clocksource drivers;\n  - Hardware crypto device drivers;\n  - CXL (Compute Express Link) drivers;\n  - Buffer Sharing and Synchronization framework;\n  - DMA engine subsystem;\n  - DPLL subsystem;\n  - EDAC drivers;\n  - FireWire subsystem;\n  - Arm Firmware Framework for ARMv8-A(FFA);\n  - ARM SCMI message protocol;\n  - GPIO subsystem;\n  - GPU drivers;\n  - HID subsystem;\n  - Microsoft Hyper-V drivers;\n  - Hardware monitoring drivers;\n  - CoreSight HW tracing drivers;\n  - I3C subsystem;\n  - InfiniBand drivers;\n  - Input Device core drivers;\n  - Input Device (Mouse) drivers;\n  - IOMMU subsystem;\n  - Media drivers;\n  - MMC subsystem;\n  - Network drivers;\n  - Mellanox network drivers;\n  - Microsoft Azure Network Adapter (MANA) driver;\n  - STMicroelectronics network drivers;\n  - Texas Instruments network drivers;\n  - Ethernet team driver;\n  - MediaTek network drivers;\n  - NTB driver;\n  - NVME drivers;\n  - Operating Performance Points (OPP) driver;\n  - PCI subsystem;\n  - Synopsys DesignWare PCIe PMU;\n  - Pin controllers subsystem;\n  - x86 platform drivers;\n  - i.MX PM domains;\n  - PTP clock framework;\n  - PWM drivers;\n  - Remote Processor subsystem;\n  - S/390 drivers;\n  - SCSI subsystem;\n  - ASPEED SoC drivers;\n  - SoundWire subsystem;\n  - SPI subsystem;\n  - Greybus lights staging